// tolerance_usecs: 4000
// Cubic starts at 1 MiB; the peer advertises 502 << 7 = 64256 bytes.
// All ten 1024-byte echoes leave before the first ACK. The four advancing
// ACKs leave six segments (6144 bytes) in flight. They send no new data.
// The third duplicate ACK triggers fast retransmit, before the 300 ms RTO.
// The duplicate ACKs arrive 50 ms apart, so a premature retransmission
// would fall outside the 4 ms tolerance. Received SACK blocks are ignored.
// Cubic sets ssthresh to floor(6144 * 0.7) = 4300 bytes, then adds three
// MSS during recovery. The full ACK deflates cwnd to 4300. Four more
// 1024-byte echoes fit (4096 bytes). A fifth 1024-byte client segment
// releases only the remaining 204 bytes, at 14337:14541. The RST ends
// the connection with 4300 echo bytes unacknowledged and 820 queued.
// Receive window 23040 units: the peer's MSS 1024 caps each of the 90 admitted frames
// (128 KiB / 1460) at 1024 bytes, 92160 bytes >> shift 2. The SYN-ACK stays 65535
// (unscaled cap); 92160 < 2 x 65535, so no window-update ACK follows the handshake.

